records.Essay Question:
Caloy (noun) died with a net estate of PHP 240,000,000.00. He was survived by the following:

1. Father — Cesar (noun);
2. Spouse — Grace (noun);
3. Legitimate children — Teddy (noun) and Bobbie (noun);
4. Illegitimate child — Rebreb (noun); and
5. Sisters — Alex (noun) and Gabbie (noun).

In his will, Caloy (noun) instituted Rebreb (noun) as his sole heir.

How much may Rebreb (noun) receive from Caloy’s (noun) estate? Explain.
